+// Fushi patch (program binary disk cache): persists ANGLE's linked programs
+// (EGL_ANDROID_blob_cache) under |directory| so later launches load them
+// instead of recompiling every Impeller pipeline. Call once, before the first
+// engine is created; |directory| must be absolute and is created on demand on
+// a background thread. The cache lives in a subfolder named after this engine
+// build; folders of other builds are deleted, total size is capped, and any
+// I/O problem (unwritable directory, full disk, damaged file) falls back to
+// compiling from source. Returns false for an invalid path or when a cache
+// with a different directory is already installed in this process.
+//
+// Engines without this patch do not export the symbol; resolve it with
+// GetProcAddress.
+FLUTTER_EXPORT bool FlutterDesktopSetProgramBinaryCacheDirectory(
+    const wchar_t* directory);
